; Regression witness for inexact modulo, remainder, and quotient contagion in
; VM native cases 36–38. The original failures collapsed integral results to
; exact values, wrapped large quotients through int64, and returned +nan.0 for
; an inexact remainder by zero. That fatal case is isolated in
; fatal/remainder_inexact_zero.esk.
; Before the repair, (exact? (quotient 7.0 2.0)) was #t,
; (quotient 1e20 3.0) was 3074457345618258602, and
; (quotient (expt 2 100) 2.0) was exact. Native returns #f,
; 33333333333333330000, and 6.338253001141147e+29 respectively.
;
; Inexact quotient truncates toward zero; every result below remains inexact.
(display (exact? (quotient -7 2)))
(newline)
(display (quotient -7 2))
(newline)
(display (exact? (quotient 7.0 2.0)))
(newline)
(display (quotient -7.0 2.0))
(newline)
(display (quotient 7.0 -2.0))
(newline)
(display (quotient -7.5 2.0))
(newline)
(display (exact? (quotient 1e20 3.0)))
(newline)
(display (quotient 1e20 3.0))
(newline)
(display (exact? (quotient (expt 2 100) 2.0)))
(newline)
(display (quotient (expt 2 100) 2.0))
(newline)
(display (exact? (modulo 5.0 3)))
(newline)
(display (exact? (modulo 5 2.0)))
(newline)
(display (exact? (remainder 5.0 3)))
(newline)
(display (modulo -5.0 3))
(newline)
(display (modulo 5.0 -3))
(newline)
(display (remainder -5.0 3))
(newline)
(display (remainder 5.0 -3))
(newline)
